<title>SINGAPORE: Keppel Land net profit up 37 percent.</title>
<headline>Keppel Land net profit up 37 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 101.60  vs  74.16</p>
<p>    Dividend (cts)		     4.00  vs   4.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)		 16.80  vs  12.90</p>
<p>    Turnover			   591.74  vs 322.28</p>
<p>    Interest &amp; other income	 46.06  vs  16.52</p>
<p>    Interest expense		  42.59  vs  22.22</p>
<p>    Depreciation			 6.12  vs   5.12</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   216.88  vs 124.41</p>
<p>    Associates			  16.95  vs  13.77</p>
<p>    Tax				   62.34  vs  27.86</p>
<p>    Minorities			 (69.90) vs (36.16)</p>
<p>Note - Keppel Land Ltd said the improved sales and profits were mainly due to its Pebble Bay condominium project and initial contributions from its Quartz and Orion industrial building projects. -- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
